From 137d172bc90bc2cd6fedb0994c091cf8631905b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niranjan Reddy Mekala <nirameka@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:51:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] virt: allow libvirt mount namespace cleanup

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/SELinuxProject/refpolicy/pull/1289]

Libvirt creates per-domain runtime mount namespaces under
/run/libvirt/qemu and mounts filesystems such as tmpfs,
devpts, hugetlbfs and device-backed filesystems.

During guest startup failure handling and domain lifecycle
cleanup, libvirt unmounts these filesystems before removing
the associated runtime directories. In SELinux enforcing
mode, the required filesystem unmount permissions are denied,
resulting in AVCs such as:

  avc: denied { unmount } for comm="rpc-libvirtd"
  scontext=system_u:system_r:virtd_t:s0

Without these permissions, libvirt cannot unmount the
per-domain runtime mounts, cleanup of runtime mount
namespaces fails, and busy mount points remain under
/run/libvirt/qemu. This can result in failures such as:

  Cannot delete directory
  /run/libvirt/qemu/<domain>.shm:
  Device or resource busy

Allow virtd_t to unmount the filesystem types observed
during libvirt runtime namespace cleanup, specifically
device_t, tmpfs_t, hugetlbfs_t and devpts_t.

Validated using libvirt, qemu-system-aarch64 and a
TPM-enabled Windows 11 ARM64 guest under SELinux
enforcing mode.

Signed-off-by: Niranjan Reddy Mekala <nirameka@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 policy/modules/services/virt.te | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/policy/modules/services/virt.te b/policy/modules/services/virt.te
index 7e6cff62b..75f108d4e 100644
--- a/policy/modules/services/virt.te
+++ b/policy/modules/services/virt.te
@@ -674,6 +674,13 @@ fs_rw_hugetlbfs_files(virtd_t)
 fs_read_nsfs_files(virtd_t)
 fs_mount_tmpfs(virtd_t)
 
+# libvirt unmounts per-domain runtime filesystems during
+# guest startup failure handling and mount namespace cleanup
+allow virtd_t device_t:filesystem unmount;
+allow virtd_t tmpfs_t:filesystem unmount;
+allow virtd_t hugetlbfs_t:filesystem unmount;
+allow virtd_t devpts_t:filesystem unmount;
+
 mls_fd_share_all_levels(virtd_t)
 mls_file_read_to_clearance(virtd_t)
 mls_file_write_to_clearance(virtd_t)
-- 
2.43.0

